waiver: harness-limit
reason: internal/interp has no allocator to count calls into — it is a
  tree-walking evaluator over Go values — so __heap_alloc_count()
  returns 0 there unconditionally, every literal reads as "no box" and
  the order this case measures is unobservable, exactly as for
  alloc_count_sees_recycling. See docs/ALLOCATION-OBSERVABLE.md.
